  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Prerequisite:\n- You have set your home instance type to public.\n- Your friend has created a friend-only instance (regardless of the status of the friend).\nIssue:\n- When logging in or \"Go Home\", you will join the friend-only instance that your friend has created. However, it will not join a friend+ instance created by a friend, in which case a new public instance will be created.\nExpectation :\n- For consistency, one of the following behaviors will be used\n1. Always create a public instance when logging in or \"Go Home\", regardless of the instance created by the friend.\n2. When logging in or \"Go Home\", if a friend has created a friend-only or friend+ instance, it will randomly join one of those instances.\n- About 2, there is no suggestion as to whether or not to join a Friend Plus instance that a friend has not created but has joined.\nAdditional Notes:\n- When a user logs in or \"Go Home\", if there are already public instances open, they are currently randomly joined to one of them.  This behavior seems to be imperfectly applied to friend-only instances, so I am providing this feedback.\nIf this behavior is as expected, it is worth clarifying.",
